From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: Avoid GCC 16.1 speculative shared_ptr bounds errors

GCC 16.1 can speculate that a shared_ptr control block disposes of a
different type. Its array-bounds pass can then report an access from
an unreachable path and fail the build with -Werror. This affects
both LogOutput and BoundMethodPack on AArch64.

Skip speculative devirtualization when building with GCC 16.1 and
libstdc++. Keep array-bounds and the other diagnostics enabled. GCC
16.2 includes the libstdc++ fix, so leave newer compilers unchanged.

Link: https://gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=122197
Link: https://gcc.gnu.org/g:b6274f4ec32dc4a8855459384ac899316e7a34f2
Assisted-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -184,6 +184,15 @@ if cc.get_id() == 'gcc'
     endif
 endif
 
+# GCC PR 122197: avoid false bounds reports from speculative shared_ptr
+# devirtualization with libstdc++ 16.1. Keep the bounds diagnostic enabled.
+if cxx.get_id() == 'gcc' and cxx_stdlib == 'libstdc++'
+    gcc_version = cxx.version()
+    if gcc_version.version_compare('>=16.1') and gcc_version.version_compare('<16.2')
+        cpp_arguments += ['-fno-devirtualize-speculatively']
+    endif
+endif
+
 # We use C99 designated initializers for arrays as C++ has no equivalent
 # feature. Both gcc and clang support this extension, but recent
 # versions of clang generate a warning that needs to be disabled.
